# R19 — the same five trajectory conditions, recorded at every optimiser step.
#
# Why. Birdal et al. estimate dim_PH on 200 *consecutive* iterates: train to convergence,
# then run 200 more steps and fit on those. Section 6.4 estimates it on 200 iterates at
# stride 20, which span 4,000 steps — not a coarser version of the same measurement but a
# different arc of the trajectory, twenty times longer, where drift dominates the local
# diffusion the fractal structure lives in. A finer sampling is not recoverable from a
# coarser recording, so the stride is the one parameter section A.6 cannot sweep, and it is
# the one deviation from the protocol being tested against.
#
# One recording at stride 1 gives both: stride 20 is a decimation of it, so the comparison
# is within-run with nothing else varying. Every line below is its twin in R12 or R13 with
# `trajectory_every` changed and the run renamed; the recorder draws its projection from its own
# generator and touches no other RNG, so recording every step does not perturb the optimisation.
# Measured: a decimated stride-one recording matches its stride-twenty twin to 1.9e-5 -- float32
# rounding in the projection -- for 2,943 of 3,001 recorded points, and diverges only over the
# last thousand steps, where accumulated GPU non-determinism finally tells. Nothing below depends
# on that agreement: every comparison here is a decimation of one recording against itself.
#
# The set is the one the correlation needs: five conditions whose measured gaps run
# 0.00, 0.07-0.71, 0.00-0.70, 0.80, 0.99, covering the range continuously.
#
# `_stride1` is already in REPLICATE_TAGS (identity.py), so these cannot pool into the
# condition table. Storage: steps x 128 x 4 bytes, so 60k steps is 30 MB; 25 runs ~ 600 MB.

# --- p=113, wd 0.1, 60k steps (gap 0.00; the reference regime) ---------------------
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_stride1_s0 seed=0 train.capture_representations=false train.n_snapshots=200 train.trajectory_dim=128 train.trajectory_every=1 train.dense_from=8000 train.dense_to=18000
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_stride1_s1 seed=1 train.capture_representations=false train.n_snapshots=200 train.trajectory_dim=128 train.trajectory_every=1 train.dense_from=8000 train.dense_to=18000
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_stride1_s2 seed=2 train.capture_representations=false train.n_snapshots=200 train.trajectory_dim=128 train.trajectory_every=1 train.dense_from=8000 train.dense_to=18000
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_stride1_s3 seed=3 train.capture_representations=false train.n_snapshots=200 train.trajectory_dim=128 train.trajectory_every=1 train.dense_from=8000 train.dense_to=18000
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_stride1_s4 seed=4 train.capture_representations=false train.n_snapshots=200 train.trajectory_dim=128 train.trajectory_every=1 train.dense_from=8000 train.dense_to=18000

